## Source Files

### `frontend/src/main.js`

- Vue app bootstrap.
- Imports Element Plus, Element Plus CSS, root `App.vue`, and global `styles.css`.
- Mounts the app to `#app`.

### `frontend/src/App.vue`

- Root UI and most application state.
- Shows password login when unauthenticated.
- Authenticated layout includes:
  - top bar with trip selector and trip create/edit/delete/logout actions;
  - left panel for trip list, current trip, places, and routes;
  - central `MapView`;
  - right panel tabs for search, place editing, and route creation;
  - Element Plus dialog for creating/editing trips.
- Owns state for trips, places, routes, selected trip/place, search results, forms, tabs, and loading flags.
- Calls API modules from `src/services/api.js`.
- Calls Baidu navigation helpers from `src/utils/navigation.js`.
- Registers `window.travelMapActions` so Baidu Map InfoWindow buttons can call back into Vue actions.
- Key functions include:
  - auth: `login`, `logout`, `resetWorkspaceState`;
  - trips: `loadTrips`, `loadTripData`, `selectTrip`, `openTripDialog`, `saveTrip`, `deleteCurrentTrip`;
  - places: `startManualPlace`, `handleMapClick`, `selectPlace`, `savePlace`, `deletePlace`, `deletePlaceById`;
  - search: `searchBaiduPlaces`, `addSearchResult`;
  - routes: `createRoute`, `autoGenerateRoutes`, `deleteRoute`, `deleteRouteById`, `navigateRoute`, `navigateFromPlace`.

### `frontend/src/components/MapView.vue`

- Baidu Map rendering and map interactions.
- Props:
  - `places`
  - `routes`
  - `selectedPlaceId`
- Emits:
  - `map-click`
  - `place-selected`
- Uses `loadBaiduMap` from `src/utils/mapLoader.js`.
- Renders:
  - Baidu map instance;
  - place markers with optional subtitle/current labels;
  - route polylines;
  - InfoWindows for places and routes;
  - error overlay when map cannot load.
- Exposes methods to parent:
  - `focusPlace(placeId)`
  - `searchPlaces(keyword)`
- Important implementation detail: InfoWindow HTML is manually escaped with `escapeHtml` because it is outside Vue template rendering.

### `frontend/src/services/api.js`

- Central Axios API client.
- Uses `appConfig.apiBaseUrl`.
- Stores auth token in `sessionStorage` under `travel-helper-auth-token`.
- Adds `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on requests when present.
- Handles `401` responses outside `/auth/login` by clearing token and invoking a registered unauthorized handler.
- Exports:
  - token helpers: `getAuthToken`, `setAuthToken`, `clearAuthToken`;
  - handler helper: `setUnauthorizedHandler`;
  - `authApi`: `login`, `validate`;
  - `tripApi`: `list`, `create`, `update`, `remove`;
  - `placeApi`: `list`, `create`, `update`, `remove`;
  - `routeApi`: `list`, `create`, `update`, `remove`.

### `frontend/src/utils/mapLoader.js`

- Lazy-loads Baidu Map JS API when `window.BMap` is not already present.
- Reuses a module-level `loadingPromise` to avoid duplicate script injection.
- Detects an existing Baidu script tag and waits for `window.BMap`.
- Rejects with user-facing Chinese error messages for missing AK, timeout, or script load failure.

### `frontend/src/utils/navigation.js`

- Defines supported route travel modes:
  - `driving` / 驾车
  - `walking` / 步行
  - `transit` / 公交
  - `riding` / 骑行
- Provides `getTravelModeLabel(mode)`.
- Builds Baidu direction URL with `buildBaiduNavigationUrl(fromPlace, toPlace, mode)`.
- Opens navigation in a new tab with `openBaiduNavigation(fromPlace, toPlace, mode)`.

### `frontend/src/config.js`

- Exports `appConfig`.
- Reads compile-time global `__APP_CONFIG__` if available.
- Falls back to:
  - app name: `旅行规划地图`;
  - API base URL: `http://localhost:3000/api`;
  - empty Baidu Map AK.

### `frontend/src/styles.css`

- Global styles for the Vue app.
- Covers login shell, app shell, top bar, left/right panels, map panel, forms, list rows, Element Plus layout adjustments, and map InfoWindow content.

## Config And Build Files

### `frontend/package.json`

- Package name: `travel-helper-frontend`.
- Scripts:
  - `pnpm dev`: starts Vite with host `0.0.0.0`;
  - `pnpm build`: runs Vite production build;
  - `pnpm preview`: previews build with host `0.0.0.0`.
- Dependencies:
  - Vue 3
  - Vite
  - Element Plus
  - Element Plus icons
  - Axios

### `frontend/vite.config.js`

- Vite configuration with Vue plugin.
- Reads `frontend/app.config.json`.
- Defines fallback config if the JSON file is missing.
- Exposes public frontend config as `__APP_CONFIG__`.
- Injects Baidu Map script into `index.html` when a Baidu AK exists.
- Dev server port comes from `app.config.json` frontend settings, defaulting to `5173`.
- Production base path is `/travel-helper/`.

### `frontend/app.config.json`

- Local app configuration shared by frontend-related setup.
- Contains frontend port/API URL, backend/database/auth/Baidu Map settings.
- Sensitive values exist in this file. Future AI work should avoid copying secrets into logs, docs, commits, or responses unless the user explicitly asks.

### `frontend/index.html`

- Vite HTML entry.
- Language: `zh-CN`.
- Mount target: `<div id="app"></div>`.
- Loads `/src/main.js`.
- Notes that Baidu Map JS API is injected by `vite.config.js`.

### `frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml`

- pnpm lockfile for reproducible dependency installation.
- Usually do not edit manually.

